                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Lots of potential, story and idea wise. However, the quality is way too bad and the game is not what I would consider as 'ready', I went in expecting that but still was dissapointed. I'd say give it some time to fix itself up and maybe when the price gets lowered depending on individual for the latter. I don't know how the pricing in relation to the episodes work but this game really isn't worth anything more than 20 bucks as of now.\n\nThat said, I do look forward to its 'completion' and am ready to get back to it when that time comes. Sadly, not at its current state. If this was a triple A game it might just be one of my all time favourites. Kudos to the Creator of this game, gifted. Hopefully the team isn't half-hearted about this. Unfortunate for the resources side.\n\nEdit: I apologise for the misunderstanding. It costs 15 bucks but what I was referring to earlier was that if the other two remaining episodes have individual cost themselves then the game won't be worth it, since this is only for episode one. However, again from what I have mentioned earlier, I don't know how the pricing in relation to the episodes work.\n\nKill-Chan: \"the reviewer forgot to mention the actual flaws of this game. well, here's a list: poor optimization, poor performance, bugs, glitches.\"",
